### Conflicting / official vs community evidence compared (2nd pass)

- Official launch (forum, 2026-09-10, author @329327/Qoder staff): "built for marathon-length autonomous tasks, the hardest knowledge work, and serious coding — at its best when using your computer." Computer Use with Desktop 0.2.3. Credit multiplier 3.2x (personal & enterprise).
- Official rate card (docs, 2026-09-21): Sonus 3.2x → **8x** (Kimi-K3 0.8x→1.4x, Cantus 3.2x → 4x, Qwen3.8-Max 0.5x, GLM-5.3 0.8x) — "the fastest consumption in the catalog", per docs narrative.
- Official complaint replies (forum moderator, Sept 2026): "Sonus is our 3.2x billing flagship… the top SOTA model in the industry; high compute multiplier by design."
- Official forum moderation + user reports: extreme consumption (400–4,000+ credits per heavy task; 8.7-min planning before first output in one report); "marathon" autonomous runs. No benchmark table was ever attached to any of these.
- Community identity speculation (forum topic "sonus、cantus是什么模型", 2026-10-22): "sonus 就是 sol，cantus 就是 fable" / "sonus：gpt-6-astr" / "cantus：Fable5.1" — three mutually inconsistent claims; none confirmed by anyone.
- Qoder docs: no model card published (docs search shows no Sonus/Cantus card; 193KB model pages absent).

